IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): PART 6, ARTICLES 30 AND 31, WITH SCHEDULES 11 AND 12 (EMPLOYMENT AND SUPPORT ALLOWANCE).
-- Layer 1. Article 30 amends the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 and article 31 the Employment and
-- Support Allowance Regulations 2013; neither is among the inputs. Every figure the Order states is a value. Where the
-- Order applies a figure "in cases falling within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017",
-- whether the case does is for those Regulations, so it is a plain input.
-- Dates: art 30 comes into force on the first day of the beneficiary's first benefit week to commence on or after
-- 6th April 2026 (art 1(3)(l)); art 31 likewise (art 1(3)(m), and art 1(4) for unearned income under universal credit):
-- uro-part1-intro.
-- Article 30(1) ("any reference in this article to a Schedule is a reference to the Schedule to the ESA Regulations 2008")
-- is a cross-reference convention and is not encoded.

§ `Article 30 -- Applicable amounts for the ESA Regulations 2008`

§§ `Articles 30(2) and (3) -- paragraph 1 of Schedule 4: prescribed amounts`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 (the Act is the one those Regulations name); Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017 Sch 2 paras 2 to 7: which conditions and cases apply is an input.
-- (2): the sums in paragraph 1 are those of paragraph 1 of Schedule 11 to this Order, except in the cases of (3);
-- (3): in those cases they are those of paragraph 2 of Schedule 11. Both paragraphs are encoded below and chosen here.
-- src:395 | (2) The sums specified in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 (prescribed amounts) shall be as set out in paragraph 1 of Schedule 11 to this Order except in cases referred to in paragraph (3).
-- src:396 | (3) In cases falling within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017, the sums specified in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the ESA Regulations 2008 shall be as set out in paragraph 2 of Schedule 11 to this Order.
@ref art 30(2), (3) (src:395-396)
GIVEN `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 30(2) and (3): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` `the claimant's age` MEANS
    IF `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`
    THEN `Sch 11 paragraph 2 (1): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` `the claimant's age`
    ELSE `Sch 11 paragraph 1 (1): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` `the claimant's age`

§§ `Articles 30(4) and (5) -- paragraph 11 of Schedule 4: premiums`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 Sch 4 paras 5, 8(1), 11; the 2017 Regulations Sch 2 paras 2 to 7: whether paragraph 5 applies, and the claimant's components, are inputs.
-- (4): the sums in paragraph 11(1) and (3) are those of paragraph 1 of Schedule 12 to this Order, except in the cases of
-- (5); (5): in those cases the sums in paragraph 11(1) alone are those of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12. In a case of (5)
-- the Order sets no sum for paragraph 11(3) (the carer premium).
-- src:397 | (4) The sums specified in paragraph 11(1) and (3) of Schedule 4 (weekly amount of premiums specified in Part 2) shall be as set out in paragraph 1 of Schedule 12 to this Order except in cases referred to in paragraph (5).
-- src:398 | (5) In cases falling within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017, the sums specified in paragraph 11(1) of Schedule 4 to the ESA Regulations 2008 shall be as set out in paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to this Order.
@ref art 30(4), (5) (src:397-398)
GIVEN `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is entitled to the support component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 30(4) and (5): the pensioner premium` `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` `the claimant is a member of a couple` `the claimant is entitled to the support component` `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component` MEANS
    IF `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`
    THEN `Sch 12 paragraph 2 (1): the pensioner premium` `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` `the claimant is a member of a couple` `the claimant is entitled to the support component` `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component`
    ELSE `Sch 12 paragraph 1 (1): the pensioner premium` `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` `the claimant is a member of a couple` `the claimant is entitled to the support component` `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component`

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 Sch 4 paras 5, 8(1), 11; the 2017 Regulations Sch 2 paras 2 to 7: whether paragraph 5 applies, and the claimant's components, are inputs.
@ref art 30(4), (5) (src:397-398)
GIVEN `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 30(4) and (5): the carer premium` `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)` MEANS
    IF `the case falls within paragraphs 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 to the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`Sch 12 paragraph 1 (3): the carer premium` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)`)

