§ `Schedule 11 to the Order -- Part 1 of Schedule 4 to the ESA Regulations 2008 (prescribed amounts)`

-- The text prints two tables under the markers "1" and "2" (paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 11, as art 30(2) and (3) call
-- them). Each prints only "(1) Single claimant"; rows for a lone parent and a couple are not in the text (fork F-07), so
-- a claimant who is not a single claimant gets no answer from this encoding.

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 (the Act; 'work-related activity group'): whether the conditions are met is an input.
-- src:733 | 1
-- src:734 | | (1) Person or Couple | (2) Amount |
-- src:735 | | (1) Single claimant— | (1) |
-- src:736 | | (a) | who satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act or who is a member of the work-related activity group; | (a) | £95.55; |
-- src:737 | | (b) | aged not less than 25; | (b) | £95.55; |
-- src:738 | | (c) | aged less than 25. | (c) | £75.65; |
@ref Sch 11 paragraph 1 (1) (src:733-738)
GIVEN `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 paragraph 1 (1): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` `the claimant's age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` OR `the claimant is a member of the work-related activity group` THEN 95.55   -- (a)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25 THEN 95.55   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE 75.65   -- (c) aged less than 25

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 (the Act; 'work-related activity group'): whether the conditions are met is an input.
