-- src:743 | | (b) | aged not less than 25; | (b) | £95.55; |
-- src:744 | | (c) | aged less than 25. | (c) | £75.65; |
@ref Sch 11 paragraph 2 (1) (src:739-744)
GIVEN `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 paragraph 2 (1): the prescribed amount for a single claimant` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` `the claimant's age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(2) of the Act` OR `the claimant satisfies the conditions set out in section 2(3) of the Act` THEN 95.55   -- (a)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25 THEN 95.55   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE 75.65   -- (c) aged less than 25

§ `Schedule 12 to the Order -- Part 3 of Schedule 4 to the ESA Regulations 2008 (weekly amounts of premiums specified in Part 2)`

-- The text prints two tables whose paragraph markers were lost in conversion. The first has the carer premium (3) and
-- lacks rows (a)(i) and (b)(i); the second has all six rows (i) to (iii) and no (3). Art 30(4) points to Schedule 12
-- paragraph 1 for paragraph 11(1) and (3), and art 30(5) to Schedule 12 paragraph 2 for paragraph 11(1) alone, so the
-- first table is taken as paragraph 1 and the second as paragraph 2 (fork F-14).
-- In the first table, row (iii) reads "is not entitled to the support component" where the second table's reads "is not
-- entitled to either of those components", and the (i) row for the work-related activity component is not printed. Read as
-- printed, a claimant who is entitled to the work-related activity component and not to the support component is within
-- row (iii) of paragraph 1, because (iii) asks only about the support component (fork F-13). Paragraph 1 therefore does
-- not look at the work-related activity component; the input is kept so that both paragraphs take the same inputs.

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 Sch 4 paras 5 and 8(1): whether paragraph 5 applies, the support and work-related activity components and couple status are inputs.
-- src:748 | | 11.—(1) Pensioner premium for a person to whom paragraph 5 applies who— | (1) |
-- src:749 | | (a) | is a single claimant and— | (a) | |
-- src:750 | | (ii) | is entitled to the support component; or | (ii) | £93.95; |
-- src:751 | | (iii) | is not entitled to the support component; | (iii) | £142.45; |
-- src:752 | | (b) | is a member of a couple and— | (b) | |
-- src:753 | | (ii) | is entitled to the support component; or | (ii) | £164.60; |
-- src:754 | | (iii) | is not entitled to the support component; | (iii) | £213.10; |
@ref Sch 12 paragraph 1 (1) (src:748-754)
GIVEN `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is entitled to the support component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 12 paragraph 1 (1): the pensioner premium` `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` `the claimant is a member of a couple` `the claimant is entitled to the support component` `the claimant is entitled to the work-related activity component` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `paragraph 5 applies to the claimant` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the claimant is entitled to the support component` AND (NOT `the claimant is a member of a couple`) THEN JUST 93.95   -- (a)(ii)
        IF `the claimant is entitled to the support component` AND `the claimant is a member of a couple` THEN JUST 164.60   -- (b)(ii)
        IF NOT `the claimant is a member of a couple` THEN JUST 142.45   -- (a)(iii)
        OTHERWISE JUST 213.10   -- (b)(iii)

-- out of text: Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008 Sch 4 paras 5 and 8(1): whether paragraph 5 applies, the support and work-related activity components and couple status are inputs.
-- src:755 | | (3) Carer Premium. | (3) £48.15 in respect of each person who satisfies the condition specified in paragraph 8(1). |
@ref Sch 12 paragraph 1 (3) (src:755)
GIVEN `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 12 paragraph 1 (3): the carer premium` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)` MEANS
    48.15 TIMES `the number of persons who satisfy the condition specified in paragraph 8(1)`

